# TextFSM template: MikroTik RouterOS 7.x
# `/routing bgp advertisements print detail where …`. Shared by
# bgp.route / bgp.community / bgp.largecommunity / bgp.aspath
# because all four queries emit the same per-advertisement block
# shape.
#
# Sample output (truncated):
#  Flags: A - active
#   0 A peer="peer1" dst-address=1.1.1.0/24
#       nexthop=10.0.0.2 origin=igp local-pref=100 med=0
#       as-path="65001,65002"
#       communities=65000:100,65000:200
#       large-communities=214503:8:3607
#
# Capture strategy:
#   - Each numbered entry is one advertisement. The leading `A`
#     flag marks the active path; absent means the path is a
#     backup. `best` is captured by an optional sub-pattern at the
#     end of the prefix-line; the projector's recBool() treats `A`
#     as truthy.
#   - `as_path` is a comma-separated decimal list inside quotes.
#     We capture the whole quoted value; the projector's
#     splitListToken() splits on commas/whitespace before integer
#     parsing.
#   - Communities and large-communities lines likewise use single
#     captures spanning the full comma-separated value list.
#   - `peer_ip` and `peer_asn` are not directly emitted by the
#     advertisements view — only the operator-defined peer name
#     is. We leave those fields zero; the wire payload still
#     carries the prefix and AS-path which is the primary intent
#     of bgp.route / bgp.community queries.
Value Required prefix ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+/\d+)
Value nexthop ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value origin (\S+)
Value local_pref (\d+)
Value med (\d+)
Value as_path (\d+(?:[,\s]+\d+)*)
Value communities (\d+:\d+(?:,\d+:\d+)*)
Value large_communities (\d+:\d+:\d+(?:,\d+:\d+:\d+)*)
Value best (A)
Value description (\S+)

Start
  ^\s*Flags:\s+A\s+-\s+active
  ^\s*\d+(?:\s+${best})?\s+peer="${description}"\s+dst-address=${prefix}
  ^\s+nexthop=${nexthop}(?:\s+origin=${origin})?(?:\s+local-pref=${local_pref})?(?:\s+med=${med})?
  ^\s+as-path="${as_path}"
  ^\s+communities=${communities}\s*$$
  ^\s+large-communities=${large_communities}\s*$$ -> Record
  ^\s*$$ -> Record
